## Plans

### Selected Plan #1 — Scissor pointer aliasing in draw flatten paths
- Sink: fz_draw_fill_path/stroke_path/clip_path/clip_stroke_path call fz_flatten_fill_path/stroke_path(ctx, rast, ..., &bbox, &bbox), passing the same fz_irect* as both scissor and bbox output. Inside fz_flatten_fill_path (draw-path.c:266-302), *bbox is written (line 300) before *scissor is read (line 301), so the aliased scissor is the overwritten bound; the return emptiness test uses bound vs bound instead of bound vs true scissor.
- Harness/route: pdf_fuzzer opens a PDF and renders every page with fz_new_pixmap_from_page_number(identity, RGB, alpha=0) -> fz_new_draw_device + fz_run_page, so page content operators (fill/stroke/clip paths, images, text) reach the aliased draw-device calls.
- Carrier: Carrier is a PDF; page pixmap/scissor derives from fz_bound_page (MediaBox), and draw-device initial scissor is the pixmap bbox. Content streams reach the aliased flatten path when they fill/stroke/clip a path.
